From: Russell Oliver <roliver8143@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 02:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] Bluetooth: SMP: distribute local identity for LE legacy OOB bonds

For devices observed in the wild (e.g., Microsoft Modern Keyboard), the device
will only persist the bond after the initiator distributes identity
information. Make the kernel include ID key distribution for pairings that use a
LE legacy OOB TK so these devices can persist bonds without manual workarounds.

This change is limited to the OOB-legacy path (le_legacy_tk_present) and
can be disabled later or gated behind a quirk.

Signed-off-by: Russell Oliver <roliver8143@gmail.com>
---
*** Begin Patch
*** Update File: net/bluetooth/smp.c
@@
 void build_pairing_cmd(struct smp *smp, u8 *cmd)
 {
     struct hci_conn *hcon = smp->hcon;
     u8 authreq = smp->authreq;
     u8 local_dist = smp->local_dist;
+    struct oob_data *oob = NULL;
 
+    /* If a legacy TK is present, include local Identity distribution so the
+     * peer receives our Identity Information & Identity Address. This helps
+     * devices that only persist a bond after the initiator sends identity. */
+    if (hcon && hcon->type == LE_LINK) {
+        oob = hci_remote_oob_data_lookup(hcon->hdev, &hcon->dst);
+        if (oob && oob->le_legacy_tk_present)
+            local_dist |= SMP_DIST_ID_KEY;
+    }
+
     if (smp->oob_present)
         authreq |= SMP_OOB_PRESENT;
*** End Patch
